<section class="framework section" id="framework"><div class="section-intro"><h2>Your idea.<br>Your way of building.</h2><p>From the first route to your next release, Inna gives you practical foundations and room to make the rest your own.</p></div><div class="feature-layout"><div class="feature-list"><article><i data-lucide="route"></i><div><h3>Give every request a home.</h3><p>Connect URLs to controllers with readable routing and named parameters.</p><a href="/documentation/the-basics/routing">Routing <i data-lucide="arrow-up-right"></i></a></div></article><article><i data-lucide="blocks"></i><div><h3>Keep your application clear.</h3><p>Models, views and controllers, with Twig handling the templates.</p><a href="/documentation/the-basics/controllers">Application structure <i data-lucide="arrow-up-right"></i></a></div></article><article><i data-lucide="shield-check"></i><div><h3>Build beyond the happy path.</h3><p>JWT authentication, middleware, validation and logging are part of the toolkit.</p><a href="/documentation/security/jwt">Security guides <i data-lucide="arrow-up-right"></i></a></div></article></div><div class="code-window"><div class="code-title"><span><b></b><b></b><b></b></span> index.php <span>PHP</span></div><pre><code><span class="muted">&lt;?php

// A home for your next idea.</span>
<span class="blue">use</span> app\Controllers\HomeController;

<span class="mint">$app</span>->router->get(
    <span class="gold">'/'</span>,
    [HomeController::<span class="blue">class</span>, <span class="gold">'home'</span>]
);

<span class="mint">$app</span>->run();</code></pre><div class="code-foot"><span class="status-dot"></span> Less between you and your application.</div></div></div></section>
